2026-10-29T14:55:40.8248104Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-29T14:55:40.8248724Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-29T14:55:40.8249087Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-29T14:55:40.8249315Z 
2026-10-29T14:55:40.8249510Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-29T14:55:40.8249768Z 
2026-10-29T14:55:40.8249982Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-29T14:55:40.8250575Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-29T14:55:40.8250747Z 
2026-10-29T14:55:40.8250834Z If you would like to
2026-10-29T14:55:40.8251070Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-29T14:55:40.8251203Z 
2026-10-29T14:55:40.8251363Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-29T14:55:40.8251645Z   $ sh ./install-nix
